<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Security Policy</title>

<style>
body{
    font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
    margin:0;
    padding:0;
    background:#f4f6f8;
    line-height:1.6;
}

header{
    background:#203a43;
    color:white;
    padding:20px;
    text-align:center;
}

.container{
    max-width:900px;
    margin:40px auto;
    background:white;
    padding:30px;
    border-radius:10px;
    box-shadow:0 5px 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);
}

h1,h2{
    color:#203a43;
}

ul{
    margin-left:20px;
}

footer{
    text-align:center;
    padding:20px;
    background:#203a43;
    color:white;
    margin-top:40px;
}

a{
    color:#203a43;
    text-decoration:none;
}
</style>
</head>

<body>

<header>
<h1>Website Security Policy</h1>
<p>Last Updated: 2026</p>
</header>

<div class="container">

<h2>1. Introduction</h2>
<p>
This website is hosted on GitHub Pages and maintained as a personal project.
The security of visitors and website content is taken seriously. This page
describes the basic security practices used to maintain the integrity of the site.
</p>

<h2>2. Secure Hosting</h2>
<p>
The website is hosted using GitHub Pages, which provides HTTPS encryption and
secure infrastructure. All data transferred between the website and visitors
is encrypted using SSL/TLS.
</p>

<h2>3. Security Measures</h2>
<p>The following security practices are implemented:</p>
<ul>
<li>HTTPS encryption for all website traffic</li>
<li>Restricted repository access for maintainers</li>
<li>Two-factor authentication for repository owners</li>
<li>Regular review of website source code</li>
<li>No storage of sensitive user information</li>
</ul>

<h2>4. Phishing Protection</h2>
<p>
Users should always verify the website URL before entering any information.
Any websites claiming to represent this project that are not linked from the
official repository should be treated as suspicious.
</p>

<h2>5. Reporting Security Issues</h2>
<p>
If you discover a security vulnerability or suspicious behavior related to
this website, please report it responsibly through the GitHub repository
or contact the website owner.
</p>

<h2>6. Responsible Disclosure</h2>
<p>
Security researchers and users who report vulnerabilities in good faith
are appreciated. All valid reports will be reviewed and addressed as
quickly as possible.
</p>

<h2>7. Disclaimer</h2>
<p>
While reasonable security practices are followed, no website or system
connected to the internet can be guaranteed to be completely secure.
Users should always follow general cybersecurity best practices when
browsing online.
</p>

<h2>8. Policy Updates</h2>
<p>
This security policy may be updated periodically to reflect improvements
in security practices or changes in website infrastructure.
</p>

</div>

<footer>
<p>© 2026 Personal Website | Hosted on GitHub Pages</p>
</footer>

</body>
</html>
